Thanks for all the advice everyone. I did change back to an elf, then
slaughtered fort Ludos which bumped my exp up sufficiently. Completed
the quest, and I'm now messing around with a polymorph trap and a
whole stack of tasty tasty rings. Gave up on the pet dragons. Until I
get me a magic whistle it's too frustrating watching them try to find
me. I think the speed boots were to blame, but the invisibility and
stealth probably doesn't help. I suppose I could bust a potion of see
invisible over his head...

BTW, what about being a centaur? They look pretty cool, and presumably
I could keep my armour (except boots).

Also, I think I prefer gauntlets of power over gauntlets of Dext: You
lose a bit of spellcastng ability but with skills, the Eye of A and
lots of good stats you hardly notice, and I like being able to carry
loads of junk without getting burdened. Just need to get me a BoH from
somewhere. Was most disappointed not to get one in either the mines or
Sobokan.

This is by far the most successful game I've ever played, and the four
things I have not yet come across at all are the four mid-level
trinkets I usually get first and rely on the most: Wand of polymorph,
spell of identify, Bag of Holding and magic whistle. I've found and
IDed almost everything else. Maybe I need to go back and quaff a few
fountains, sooner or later I might get to wish for one.

